            <div xml:id="d628">

                <pb facs="0879" n="765" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg765"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1429: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Culbertson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-15T15:00:00-05:00">October 15, 1931—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>48. Your 128, October 14, 5 [<hi rendition="#italic">11</hi>] p.m., third
                    paragraph. Department does not desire you to visit Bolivia or Paraguay at this
                    time.</p>
                <pb facs="0880" n="766" xml:id="pg766"/>
                <p>I much appreciate the action which Señor Izquierdo has taken in this matter and
                    would like to have you express to him my personal thanks for his interest in the
                    matter. Please tell him that Señor Cruchaga has also been very helpful.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
